    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d411">

                <pb facs="0439" n="341" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg341"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Executive Agreement Series No. 37</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Unilateral Declaration of the Foreign Signatories to
                        the Chinese Minister for Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">C. T.
                        Wang</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking, China</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-02-17">February 17, 1930</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: With reference to the Agreement
                    which we have signed today establishing a new Chinese judicial system in the
                    International Settlement at Shanghai, we desire to point out that such Agreement
                    cannot in any way affect or invalidate rights guaranteed to the Powers concerned
                    and to their nationals under existing treaties between such Powers and China and
                    we accordingly reserve our full rights in this regard.</p>
                <p>We further reserve the right to object to the enforcement in the International
                    Settlement of any future Chinese laws that affect or in any way invalidate the
                    Land Regulations or Bye-Laws of the International Settlement or that may be
                    considered prejudicial to the maintenance of peace and order within this
                    area.</p>
                <p>We avail ourselves [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. de Pinto Diaz</hi></signed><lb/>on
                    behalf of the Brazilian Chargé d’Affaires<lb/>In the name of the American
                            Minister,<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph E.
                        Jacobs</hi></signed><lb/><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Meyrick
                    Hewlett</hi><lb/>on behalf of His Britannic Majesty’s Minister<lb/><signed><hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">L. Gronvold</hi></signed><lb/>on behalf of the
                    Norwegian Chargé d’Affaires<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. E. H.
                            Groenman</hi></signed><lb/>on behalf of the Netherlands chargé
                    d’affaires<lb/>In the name of the French Minister:<lb/><signed><hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">E. Koechlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
